\f0\fs22 He felt\'85 well, awkward. He\'92d been surrounded by survivors of the sickness that struck so many Elvi at 
\fs20 GET BENT
\fs22 . He\'92d never felt the need to say anything important before, and regarded the need now as the kind of hassle he\'92d only ever felt in conversations with estranged relatives at UNSAC Day marches. He gravitated towards Elvi he knew; people who knew him would expect nothing from him. Mostly, that meant Elvines he\'92d slept with, which created a whole other dimension of awkward as the Elvines eyed off his entourage of Elvisettes (only the Great Teacher was allowed to invite Elvisettes). Most of them turned out to have been at Bent Street too, which added yet another dimension of awkward as they seemed to expect some consoling words from him as Great Teacher. Strangely, his offers to hook up later just seemed to make things worse.\
Chanta searched his low-performing skull for the words that any decent great teacher might say at times like these, and come up with, \'93Evolution will work it out in the end.\'94\
\'93Praise the Dawkins,\'94 one mourner intoned.\
\'93And the One After the One,\'94 into another.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 We won\'92t praise the Dawkins
\f0\i0 , Chanta muttered under his breath. Fortunately no one heard him; that was an argument even Chanta could figure out had passed beyond his winning.\
Awkward.\
Chanta was saved by the Chief of Staff of the High Elvis-elect circulating among the guests, followed by a noticeable drift trending to a crush of guests at the bar. \'93If everyone cold take their places,\'94 the Chief of Staff said. \'93We\'92re about to begin.\'94 She noticed Chanta\'92s pained looked at the standing room only between him and a drink, and put her hand on his shoulder. \'93I\'92ll make sure we send over something nice,\'94 she reassured and smiled.\
Walter was still in Chanta\'92s throne, casting out territorial stare that said, 
\f2\i I\'92m the mayor of GET BENT, and I don\'92t care even if you are the Great Preacher or whatever they call you.
\f0\i0 \
Chanta waved the kid\'92s resting Fight Club face down. \'93Stay, there,\'94 he said, and sat on the edge of the dais. It was about as close to Sarah as he could get without his limbs turning to jack cheese, and it allowed his Elvisettes to huddle closer. Some sat on the dais; some sat on the floor at his feet. Tax! One removed his shoes and massaged his feet. He was glad he\'92d changed his socks that morning.\
Kathy tapped Chanta on the shoulder. \'93Those Elvines you were talking to before\'97you know them?\'94\
\'93Sure. I know a lot of Elvines, Kathy.\'94\
Kathy pursed her lips as she watched the group Chanta had been talking with. \'93They\'92re looking\'85  well.\'94\
Chanta nodded. \'93A guess I just make them happy. They say I make them laugh.\'94\
Kathy had to credit that. People did tend to laugh around Chanta. \'93How many of them have you laughed all the way into bed?\'94\
\'93Kathy, are you jealous?\'94\
Even Hayley laughed at that.\
\'93Hey!\'94 Chanta was offended. \'93I\'92m the Great Teacher and possibly the richest cleaner in the history of the world.\'94\
\'93Your old friends like you better when you were neither.\'94\
Chant shrugged. \'93I still like you, Kathy, even if you like someone else more now.\'94\
Kathy counted the busted globes in the chandeliers. \'93Is it all of them? Have you slept with all of them?\'94\
Sarah was all thin lips and hands on belly. She and Kathy watched Chanta as he surveyed \
\
\
The house lights went down and three spots focussed on the spa bath where a Clambake-series Elvis called Tom Wilson climbed two wooden steps that had been screwed to the side of the spa bath and stood on the mosaics, where the mermaids had been looking world-weary since before anybody in the room was born.\
\'93My fellow Elvi,\'94 Tom said. \'93Praise the Dawkins.\'94\

\f2\i Praise the Dawkins! Bless the Holy Momma!\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0 \cf2 Chant ground his teeth.
\f2\i \

\f0\i0 \'93We are all equal under Evolution,\'94 Tom declared. \'93The Airborne, the Cloudborne, and the descendants of the clones. We are the survivors, we are the fittest.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 We are the survivors, we are the fittest. It is meet and right to be so.\
