\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 The ceremony ended and the room did not empty, because nothing in the Clambake ever emptied. It redistributed. It went from a room facing one way to a room facing every way at once, and the two currents that mattered ran between the spa bath and the bar and met head on halfway, so that anybody carrying a full glass through the middle of it was carrying a wet shirt home.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 It was a wake and it was a coronation and nobody had told the room which one to be, so it was being both a few metres apart. Two Blue Hawaiis laughed so hard that one had to take hold of the other\u8217 ?s sleeve. Close enough to touch them, a Tulsa wept into a beer with somebody\u8217 ?s hand flat on the back of his neck, and neither party found the other odd.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Sarah stayed in the chair. Standing up was a project with stages and an audience, and there was no need, because the room came to her. They arrived in ones and twos with their hands already half out, and every second one wanted the belly, and about a third asked first.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy went into the crowd.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Hayley went up the stairs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 She went up because she had spent a career in rooms and had never once learned anything useful from the middle of one. The staircase was occupied to the turn and she went up it sideways, and the mezzanine was occupied too \u8212 ? Elvi who had not seen a minute of the ceremony and had cheered all of it \u8212 ? but there was a place at the balustrade near the corner where the secret rooms started, and from there she could see the floor.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 What you could see from the floor was a wall of people. What you could see from up there was where the wall opened.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 It opened for the Great Teacher. He came out of the crush below her with his sunglasses throwing light at the ceiling, and the room folded back off him the way water goes off a bow, and closed again behind him, and the closing was the interesting part, because it did not close on everybody. A wake of people came through with him and were let through, and the same wake went back the other way a few minutes later, and then again.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 He was drinking fast. Hayley worked out why on the second crossing: he had two in his hands and no way through the middle without wearing them, so he put them down his neck where he stood, and then he was a man with nothing in his hands at a bar he had just left. Nobody would let him buy one. That was the whole trouble. Every Elvis between the dais and the taps wanted the honour, so the moment he arrived he had two again, and the moment he wanted to sit down he had to get rid of them, and the apparatus wound him back and forth across that floor like a toy on a track.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 The people who came with him were not the same people every time. That was the other thing you could only see from above. Somebody would peel off at the bar and stay there talking, and two more would attach themselves on the way back, and by the fourth crossing there were faces in his wake that had been standing over by the curtains all night.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Down on the floor, Kathy was getting sleeves pushed up.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 She had not come with a plan. She had come to a wake with a bag she had not opened, carrying a thing at the back of her head that had been sitting there since Bent Street and had never once arranged itself into a question. Pieces in a drawer. What she had found in the blood of the dead, and what she had never found in the blood of anybody who was well \u8212 ? for the plain reason that nobody who is well ever gives you any. Well people do not come to doctors. In the whole of her working life she had never once stood in a room with a hundred of them at the same time.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 She was standing in one now.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 A Clambake with grey coming through his sideburns got himself up off the chesterfield in three separate movements, with a hand on the arm of it and a noise. Two paces further on an Elvine came off a bar stool and stood a moment with her palm pressed flat into the small of her back, waiting for something to finish. Nobody looked at either of them. In that room it was weather.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Then Rusty Martin came off a low stool in one go, still talking, and went to the bar.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy did not stop walking. Her head turned, though, and stayed turned a beat past where it had any business.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Maile Duval had her sleeve pushed up past the elbow and her arm out and a small audience for it, and she was delighted with herself.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?[ ] years,\u8221 ? she was saying. \u8220 ?[ ] years I\u8217 ?ve had that, and I went to a man in Bent Street about taking it off and he told me it\u8217 ?d cost more than the wedding did.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Let me,\u8221 ? said Kathy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Maile put the arm into her hands with the satisfaction of a woman who has finally found somebody qualified to agree with her. There had been a name on the inside of the forearm once, done in the ornate lettering that takes a good hand and a long sitting. It was a grey suggestion now. The heavy work at the edges had held on better than the rest, so what was left was an outline with the middle gone out of it, like a word rubbed off a blackboard by somebody in a hurry.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?When did it start going?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?That\u8217 ?s what I can\u8217 ?t tell you. I looked at his name every morning of my life, and then one morning I\u8217 ?m at the sink and I think, hang on.\u8221 ? She turned the wrist over. \u8220 ?Best thing that\u8217 ?s happened to me all year, and I\u8217 ?m counting walking out of Bent Street.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy turned the arm slightly, into the light off the bar, and did not let go of it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Any scars?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?What?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Anything you\u8217 ?ve had a long time. Old ones.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Maile thought about it, and then pushed the sleeve the rest of the way up, to a place above the elbow where there was nothing whatever to see, and looked at the nothing for a while with a different face on.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Huh,\u8221 ? she said.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy gave the arm back, gently, and was already looking past her, because it was not the same on all of them. The woman beside Maile Duval had a forearm you could still read. Dianne Carter, two along, had one you would have to be told was there at all. Some of them were further into whatever it was than the others, and there was nothing in a single face in that group to say which.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Dianne Carter had been watching her do it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Go on then,\u8221 ? she said.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?I\u8217 ?m not doing anything.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?You\u8217 ?re doing something.\u8221 ? She was not shouting. It was worse than shouting. \u8220 ?Do you know what I\u8217 ?ve been doing since Bent Street? Going to funerals in perfect health. I\u8217 ?ve been the healthiest thing at [ ] of them. Cousins of mine are in the ground and I have never felt better in my life and nobody will tell me why, and now here\u8217 ?s Aunt Kathy going up and down the room looking at everybody\u8217 ?s arms.\u8221 ? She put her own out, palm up, in front of Kathy\u8217 ?s face. \u8220 ?So go on. Is it us? Are we next?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Kathy had never in her life pretended to an answer she did not have, so she took the arm and looked at it properly, and what she found in the crook of it was skin like the inside of a shell.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 That was when the Great Teacher arrived at the bar behind them, on a crossing, with two he had not asked for.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?G\u8217 ?day,\u8221 ? said Chanta. He looked round at the group by the curtains, at Dianne Carter with her arm still out and Kathy still holding it, at the whole miserable knot of them, and he reached for something consoling and came up with the truth. \u8220 ?You\u8217 ?re all looking well.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 It went down like a dropped tray.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?I only meant \u8212 ?\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?We know what you meant, love,\u8221 ? said Maile Duval.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Chanta retreated into his beer. It was, he reflected, the worst room he had ever been in, and he had once cleaned a nightclub after a stabbing.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 Hayley came down off the stairs and put her back against the bar next to Kathy and said nothing for a while, which was how Kathy knew there was something.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?Say it,\u8221 ? said Kathy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?The same ones go across with him every time.\u8221 ? Hayley was watching the floor, not Kathy. \u8220 ?Not the same exactly. It changes. But there\u8217 ?s a set of them, and the curtains lot are in it, and his girls are in it, and it\u8217 ?s been the same set all night.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?They were at Bent Street.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?So were a lot of people who aren\u8217 ?t here.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 \u8220 ?They were at Bent Street,\u8221 ? said Kathy, \u8220 ?and they\u8217 ?re the only people in this room you\u8217 ?d look at twice.\u8221 ?\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\i0\fs22 \cf2 She reached in under the lab coat, flat against her belly, for the thing that got her through rooms, and she stopped with her hand there, because she was looking at a group of people who had been on their feet since the middle of the afternoon and had not once put a hand on a table.\
